<div class="chapter"><div class="chapter-number">Chapter 5</div><h2>Nutrition</h2><p>Real Food &middot; No Chemicals &middot; No Supplements</p></div>
<div class="quote-box">
  <p>&ldquo;Protein powders are not a good option for teens and can even be dangerous if used when dehydrated. Creatine has not been sufficiently researched in people under 18.&rdquo;</p>
  <div class="attribution">&mdash; Cleveland Clinic, Sports Health</div>
</div>
<div class="stat-row">
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">~1g</div><div class="lbl">Protein per lb bodyweight</div></div>
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">300-500</div><div class="lbl">Extra calories/day</div></div>
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">3+2</div><div class="lbl">Meals + snacks daily</div></div>
</div>
<h3>Protein Sources</h3>
