<div class="chapter"><div class="chapter-number">Chapter 7</div><h2>YouTube Video Research</h2><p>Science-Based Channels Analyzed</p></div>
<h3>#1 Hybrid Calisthenics &mdash; Hampton Liu</h3>
<p><strong>4.46M subs.</strong> Best for beginners. Free routine at hybridcalisthenics.com/routine breaks every exercise into 10-11 progressive levels with specific rep standards.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Video</th><th>Key Insights</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr><td>Push-Up Progressions<br><small>youtube.com/watch?v=zkU6Ok44_CI</small></td><td>11 levels: Wall &rarr; Incline &rarr; Knee &rarr; Full &rarr; Narrow &rarr; Staggered &rarr; Archer &rarr; One-Arm. Standard: 3&times;25 full push-ups before advancing.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Pull-Up Progressions<br><small>youtube.com/watch?v=fO3dKSQayfg</small></td><td>10 levels: Wall &rarr; Horizontal &rarr; Jackknife &rarr; Full &rarr; Narrow &rarr; One-Arm. Start at Australian rows if you can't pull-up yet.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Squat Progressions<br><small>youtube.com/watch?v=z3XQ7T4-abQ</small></td><td>10 levels: Jackknife &rarr; Assisted &rarr; Half &rarr; Full &rarr; Narrow &rarr; Pistol. Full ROM is priority.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<div class="quote-box">
  <p>&ldquo;A chain is only as strong as its weakest link. Strengthen your arms first &mdash; they're usually the weak link in both pushing and pulling.&rdquo;</p>
  <div class="attribution">&mdash; Hampton Liu</div>
</div>
<h3>#2 Calisthenicmovement</h3>
<p><strong>4.28M subs.</strong> Anatomy-based technique breakdowns. Key insight: scapular positioning is the foundation of both push-ups and pull-ups.</p>
<h3>#3 Minus The Gym &mdash; Ryan Sadilek</h3>
<p><strong>602K subs.</strong> ACE-certified, 20 yrs experience. Key video &ldquo;Beginner Calisthenics Workout At Home&rdquo; (5.1M views) uses your exact equipment setup. Also has full L-sit progression and handstand tutorial.</p>
<h3>#4 Kboges &mdash; Kyle Boggeman</h3>
<p>High-frequency, low-volume: 2 sets per exercise daily, never to failure, keep workouts 20-30 min.</p>
<h3>#5 THENX &mdash; Chris Heria</h3>
<p><strong>7.84M subs.</strong> Best for motivation. &ldquo;Six Moves to Master Calisthenics&rdquo; covers all basics.</p>
<h4>Quick Reference</h4>
<table><thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>Watch</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr><td>Full beginner routine</td><td>Hybrid Calisthenics &mdash; How to Start series</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Learning pull-ups</td><td>Minus The Gym &mdash; Beginner workout</td></tr>
  <tr><td>L-sit on parallettes</td><td>Minus The Gym &mdash; L-Sit Progression</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Handstand</td><td>Minus The Gym &mdash; Learn the Handstand</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Squat progression</td><td>Hybrid Calisthenics &mdash; squats page</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Daily practice</td><td>Kboges &mdash; training philosophy</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<div class="divider">&loz; &loz; &loz;</div>

<div class="chapter"><div class="chapter-number">Chapter 8</div><h2>Tracking &amp; Expectations</h2></div>
<h3>When to Advance</h3>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li>Hit top of rep range 2 sessions in a row &rarr; harder variation</li>
  <li>Can't hit bottom of range &rarr; easier variation</li>
  <li>Sore &gt;2 days &rarr; reduce volume</li>
  <li>Sharp joint pain &rarr; stop, check form</li>
</ul>
<h3>Realistic Timeline</h3>
<div class="stat-row">
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">Month 1</div><div class="lbl">Form improves &middot; Strength jumps</div></div>
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">Month 2-3</div><div class="lbl">Muscle definition &middot; First pull-ups</div></div>
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">Month 4-6</div><div class="lbl">Size change &middot; 5+ pull-ups &middot; 15+ dips</div></div>
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">Year 1</div><div class="lbl">Complete transformation</div></div>
</div>
<h3>The 8 Rules</h3>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Form over everything.</strong></li>
  <li><strong>Eat enough.</strong> You're 13, growing AND building muscle.</li>
  <li><strong>Sleep 8-10 hours.</strong> Non-negotiable.</li>
  <li><strong>Close to failure, not to failure.</strong></li>
  <li><strong>Consistency beats intensity.</strong></li>
  <li><strong>Drink 2-3L water daily.</strong></li>
  <li><strong>No ego.</strong> Be patient.</li>
  <li><strong>Listen to your body.</strong></li>
</ol>
<div class="quote-box">
  <p>At 13, your testosterone is naturally rising. This is the best time to start. Train smart, eat real food, let puberty + hard work do the rest.</p>
</div>
<div class="divider">&loz; &loz; &loz;</div>
<div style="text-align:center;padding:40px 0 20px;border-top:2px solid var(--accent);">
  <p style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--text-light);">The best time to start was yesterday.</p>
  <p style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--accent);">The second best time is now.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

